type RequestClearing extends CorrectableRequestMessage: <"A message sent to request the clearing of a trade or portfolio. It may include references to portfolios, trading events, valuation details, and relevant parties. The request can also include a de-clearing instruction. A message requesting that a trade be cleared by a clearing service.">
    [rootType]

    portfolioReference PortfolioReference (0..1) <"Provides the portfolio identification under which individual messages are grouped and may be acted upon collectively.">
    tradePackage TradePackage (0..1) <"A structured collection of related trades grouped under a common package. It includes a package header for metadata, multiple trade instances or references, and optional elements for allocations and approvals. This element facilitates efficient management of complex trading strategies, block trades, or multi-leg transactions by encapsulating all relevant trade details within a single package.">
    originatingEvent OriginatingEvent (0..1) <"Specifies the underlying event that triggered the creation of a trade. It is defined as a coded value based on an external scheme, allowing for standardized classification of trade origins, such as novations, amendments, or corporate actions. This element helps track the trade lifecycle by linking it to its originating context.">
    trade Trade (0..1) <"The details of a financial transaction between parties. It encapsulates key information such as product terms, counterparties, pricing, and execution details. This element serves as the foundational unit of financial contracts, supporting various trade events and lifecycle actions within the FpML framework.">
    additionalEvent AdditionalEvent (0..1)
    deClear DeClear (0..1) <"A structure describing a declear event. The deClear event allows a firm to request that a trade be removed from clearing, or a clearing service to request consent for this, or to report that it has been done.">
    quote BasicQuotation (0..*) <"Pricing information for the trade.">
    party Party (1..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

    condition Choice:
        if tradePackage exists
        then originatingEvent is absent
                and trade is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and deClear is absent
        else if trade exists
        then tradePackage is absent and additionalEvent is absent and deClear is absent
        else if additionalEvent exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and trade is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and deClear is absent
        else if deClear exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and trade is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
        else False

type RequestClearingRetracted extends NonCorrectableRequestMessage: <"A notification indicating the withdrawal of a previously submitted clearing request. It may reference trading events, de-clearing instructions, and relevant parties involved in the original request. A message withdrawing a request that a trade be cleared by a clearing service.">
    [rootType]

    tradePackage TradePackage (0..1) <"A structured collection of related trades grouped under a common package. It includes a package header for metadata, multiple trade instances or references, and optional elements for allocations and approvals. This element facilitates efficient management of complex trading strategies, block trades, or multi-leg transactions by encapsulating all relevant trade details within a single package.">
    originatingEvent OriginatingEvent (0..1) <"Specifies the underlying event that triggered the creation of a trade. It is defined as a coded value based on an external scheme, allowing for standardized classification of trade origins, such as novations, amendments, or corporate actions. This element helps track the trade lifecycle by linking it to its originating context.">
    trade Trade (0..1) <"The details of a financial transaction between parties. It encapsulates key information such as product terms, counterparties, pricing, and execution details. This element serves as the foundational unit of financial contracts, supporting various trade events and lifecycle actions within the FpML framework.">
    additionalEvent AdditionalEvent (0..1)
    deClear DeClear (0..1) <"A structure describing a declear event. The deClear event allows a firm to request that a trade be removed from clearing, or a clearing service to request consent for this, or to report that it has been done.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

    condition Choice:
        if trade exists
        then tradePackage is absent and additionalEvent is absent and deClear is absent
        else if additionalEvent exists
        then trade is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and deClear is absent
        else if deClear exists
        then trade is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
        else trade is absent
            and additionalEvent is absent
            and deClear is absent
            and originatingEvent is absent

type ClearingAcknowledgement extends EventRequestAcknowledgement: <"A response message confirming receipt of a clearing request. It may include the original request details, trade reference information, and relevant parties.">
    [rootType]

type ClearingException extends Exception: <"A message indicating an issue or error related to the clearing process. It includes an exception header, validation details, and optional correlation and exception tracking information.">
    [rootType]

type ClearingRefused extends NotificationMessage: <"A notification indicating that a clearing request has been declined. It may reference trading events, valuation details, involved parties, and reasons for refusal. A message indicating that a clearing request has not been acted on due to a business decision and therefore no trade has been cleared.">
    [rootType]

    tradePackage TradePackage (0..1) <"A structured collection of related trades grouped under a common package. It includes a package header for metadata, multiple trade instances or references, and optional elements for allocations and approvals. This element facilitates efficient management of complex trading strategies, block trades, or multi-leg transactions by encapsulating all relevant trade details within a single package.">
    originatingEvent OriginatingEvent (0..1) <"Specifies the underlying event that triggered the creation of a trade. It is defined as a coded value based on an external scheme, allowing for standardized classification of trade origins, such as novations, amendments, or corporate actions. This element helps track the trade lifecycle by linking it to its originating context.">
    trade Trade (0..1) <"The details of a financial transaction between parties. It encapsulates key information such as product terms, counterparties, pricing, and execution details. This element serves as the foundational unit of financial contracts, supporting various trade events and lifecycle actions within the FpML framework.">
    additionalEvent AdditionalEvent (0..1)
    quote BasicQuotation (0..*) <"Pricing information for the trade.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">
    reason Reason (0..*) <"Provides details on why a clearing request was refused.">

    condition Choice:
        if trade exists
        then tradePackage is absent and additionalEvent is absent
        else if additionalEvent exists
        then trade is absent and tradePackage is absent and originatingEvent is absent
        else trade is absent and additionalEvent is absent and originatingEvent is absent

type ClearingStatus extends NotificationMessage: <"A message providing an update on the status of a clearing request. It may include details about the current clearing status and involved parties. A message providing the current status of a clearing request. The Clearing Status message is designed to be sent from the Clearing House to the participants. The message sends the clearing status of the trade or the trade package. It’s a centralized model so there is no perspective.">
    [rootType]

    clearingStatusItem ClearingStatusItem (0..1) <"Describes the status of the clearing process relating to the identified trade.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

type ClearingConfirmed extends NotificationMessage: <"A notification confirming the successful completion of a clearing process. It may include details on compression, portfolio references, clearing results or trade changes, valuation information, credit limit updates, and relevant parties. A message indicating that a clearing request has been acted on and as a result a trade has been cleared.">
    [rootType]

    compressionActivity CompressionActivity (0..1) <"Compression information for the trade.">
    portfolioReference PortfolioReference (0..1) <"Provides the portfolio identification under which individual messages are grouped and may be acted upon collectively.">
    tradePackage TradePackage (0..1) <"A structured collection of related trades grouped under a common package. It includes a package header for metadata, multiple trade instances or references, and optional elements for allocations and approvals. This element facilitates efficient management of complex trading strategies, block trades, or multi-leg transactions by encapsulating all relevant trade details within a single package.">
    originatingEvent OriginatingEvent (0..1) <"Specifies the underlying event that triggered the creation of a trade. It is defined as a coded value based on an external scheme, allowing for standardized classification of trade origins, such as novations, amendments, or corporate actions. This element helps track the trade lifecycle by linking it to its originating context.">
    trade Trade (0..1) <"The details of a financial transaction between parties. It encapsulates key information such as product terms, counterparties, pricing, and execution details. This element serves as the foundational unit of financial contracts, supporting various trade events and lifecycle actions within the FpML framework.">
    additionalEvent AdditionalEvent (0..1)
    terminatingEvent TerminatingEvent (0..1) <"This may be used to describe why a trade was terminated.">
    termination TradeNotionalChange (0..1) <"Captures the terminations in the trade’s notional value. It reports a change in the size or price of a trade down to zero as part of the clearing process.">
    deClear DeClear (0..1) <"A structure describing a declear event. The deClear event allows a firm to request that a trade be removed from clearing, or a clearing service to request consent for this, or to report that it has been done.">
    clearing Clearing (0..1) <"A structure describing the registration of a trade with a clearing service as part of the clearing process.">
    change TradeChangeContent (0..1) <"Provides details of a non-negotiated trade change resulting from a market event and reported with confirmation of the completed clearing request.">
    quote BasicQuotation (0..*) <"Pricing information for the trade.">
    creditLimitInformation CreditLimitInformation (0..*) <"Provides details about the credit limits applicable to a cleared trade. This element ensures that clearing participants are informed about how the trade impacts credit exposure, which is essential for risk management and regulatory compliance.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

    condition Choice:
        if trade exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and termination is absent
                and deClear is absent
                and clearing is absent
                and change is absent
        else if additionalEvent exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and termination is absent
                and deClear is absent
                and clearing is absent
                and change is absent
        else if termination exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and deClear is absent
                and clearing is absent
                and change is absent
        else if deClear exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and clearing is absent
                and change is absent
        else if clearing exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and change is absent
        else originatingEvent is absent and terminatingEvent is absent and change is absent
            or tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent

type RequestAllocation extends CorrectableRequestMessage: <"A message requesting the allocation of a block trade into individual allocations. It includes references to related parties, the block trade identifier, allocation details, and involved parties and accounts. A message requesting that a trade be split among several accounts.">
    [rootType]

    relatedParty RelatedParty (0..*) <"Identifies a related party performing a role within the transaction.">
    blockTradeIdentifier TradeIdentifier (1..1) <"Specifies a block trade in the context of the request for allocation. A block trade refers to a large trade order that is usually too large to be executed in the open market without significantly impacting the price, causing them to often being broken into smaller portions and allocated across different accounts or parties after execution.">
    allocations Allocations (1..1) <"Represents how the block trade is divided or allocated among different accounts or parties. That is, how much of the total block trade is assigned to each party or account after the trade is executed.">
    party Party (1..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

type RequestAllocationRetracted extends NonCorrectableRequestMessage: <"A notification message indicating the withdrawal of a previously submitted allocation request. It may include the block trade identifier, allocation details, and relevant parties. A message withdrawing a request that a trade be split among several accounts.">
    [rootType]

    blockTradeIdentifier TradeIdentifier (0..1) <"Specifies a block trade that is being retracted or canceled. A block trade refers to a large trade order that is usually too large to be executed in the open market without significantly impacting the price, causing them to often being broken into smaller portions and allocated across different accounts or parties after execution.">
    allocations Allocations (0..1) <"Represent the allocated portions, previously assigned to one or more parties, that are no longer valid or need to be rolled back.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

type AllocationAcknowledgement extends EventRequestAcknowledgement: <"A response message confirming receipt of an allocation request. It may include the original request details, trade reference information, and involved parties.">
    [rootType]

type AllocationException extends Exception: <"A message indicating an issue or error in the allocation process. It includes an exception header, validation details, and optional correlation and exception tracking information.">
    [rootType]

type AllocationRefused extends ResponseMessage: <"A response indicating that an allocation request has been declined. It may include the block trade identifier, allocation details, involved parties, and reasons for refusal. A message indicating that a request to allocate a trade has been refused by the sender.">
    [rootType]

    blockTradeIdentifier TradeIdentifier (0..1) <"Uniquely identifies a block trade that was rejected for allocation. It references the original block trade that was supposed to be split among multiple accounts, and helps trace the failed allocation attempt, allowing parties to investigate and correct any issues.">
    allocations Allocations (0..1) <"Represents the allocation details of a block trade that was not accepted. It lists the intended allocations that were rejected and records them, which can be useful for troubleshooting and regulatory reporting.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">
    reason Reason (0..*) <"Describes the nature and possible location of an error in the previous message that resulted in refusal of the trade allocation request.">

type AllocationApproved extends ResponseMessage: <"A response message confirming the successful approval of an allocation request. It may include the block trade identifier, allocation details, and involved parties. A message indicating that a request to allocate a trade has been approved by the sender.">
    [rootType]

    blockTradeIdentifier TradeIdentifier (0..1) <"Uniquely identifies a block trade, which is a large transaction executed as a single trade but later allocated among multiple accounts or parties.">
    allocations Allocations (0..1) <"Contains details on how a block trade is split among different parties or accounts.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

type RequestCollateralAllocation extends CorrectableRequestMessage: <"A request message for allocating collateral between counterparties. It specifies the requested action, the collateral giver, proposed allocations, and relevant parties and accounts. Represents a request for allocating collateral in the context of financial transactions. It specifies the action to be taken regarding collateral allocation, along with relevant references and proposed details for the allocation.">
    [rootType]

    serviceName NormalizedString (0..1) <"The name of the service to which the message applies">
    requestedAction RequestedCollateralAllocationAction (0..1) <"The type of change requested for the collateral allocation.">
    collateralGiverPartyReference PartyReference (1..1) <"The party paying the margin / issuing the allocation request.">
    collateralAllocation ProposedCollateralAllocation (1..*) <"Allocation details">
    party Party (1..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

type CollateralAllocationAcknowledgement extends Acknowledgement: <"A confirmation message indicating receipt of a collateral allocation request. It may include the original request details and references to involved parties and accounts.">
    [rootType]

type CollateralAllocationRejected extends Exception: <"A message indicating that a collateral allocation request has been rejected due to an issue or validation failure. It includes exception details, validation results, and correlation information.">
    [rootType]

type CollateralAllocationAccepted extends ResponseMessage: <"A response confirming the approval and acceptance of a collateral allocation request. No additional elements are required beyond the standard response structure. Represents a confirmation message indicating that a collateral allocation has been successfully accepted. This message is part of the post-trade collateral management process, confirming that an allocation request has been successfully processed and recorded.">
    [rootType]

type OptionExpirationNotification extends ExecutionNotification: <"A notification regarding the expiration of an option, detailing trading events, amendments, regulatory collateralization, and relevant parties and accounts.">
    [rootType]

type Clearing: <"A structure describing a trade registration event that is part of a clearing process.">

    submitted TradeWrapper (1..1) <"The original trade or event submitted to the clearing service.">
    cleared TradeWrapper (2..2) <"The trades or events generated by the clearing service as a result of clearing.">

type ConfirmationRetracted extends NonCorrectableRequestMessage: <"A message indicating that a confirmation request has been withdrawn by the submitter.">

    tradePackage TradePackage (0..1) <"A structured collection of related trades grouped under a common package. It includes a package header for metadata, multiple trade instances or references, and optional elements for allocations and approvals. This element facilitates efficient management of complex trading strategies, block trades, or multi-leg transactions by encapsulating all relevant trade details within a single package.">
    originatingEvent OriginatingEvent (0..1) <"Specifies the underlying event that triggered the creation of a trade. It is defined as a coded value based on an external scheme, allowing for standardized classification of trade origins, such as novations, amendments, or corporate actions. This element helps track the trade lifecycle by linking it to its originating context.">
    trade Trade (0..1) <"The details of a financial transaction between parties. It encapsulates key information such as product terms, counterparties, pricing, and execution details. This element serves as the foundational unit of financial contracts, supporting various trade events and lifecycle actions within the FpML framework.">
    amendment TradeAmendmentContent (0..1) <"Records modifications to an existing trade, specifying the updated trade details, agreement terms, and any related payments or notional changes.">
    increase TradeNotionalChange (0..1) <"Reflects a change in the trade\'s notional amount or size, capturing adjustments to its economic terms, including price and quantity modifications.">
    terminatingEvent TerminatingEvent (0..1) <"This may be used to describe why a trade was terminated.">
    termination TradeNotionalChange (0..1) <"Documents the full or partial closure of a trade, reducing or eliminating its notional exposure, often due to settlement, early closeout, or expiration.">
    novation TradeNovationContent (0..1) <"Represents the transfer of a trade from one counterparty to another, detailing the original and new trades, fees, payment obligations, and updated contractual terms.">
    withdrawal Withdrawal (0..1) <"Indicates the removal or cancellation of a trade from reporting or processing systems, including identifiers, reasons, effective date, and requested actions.">
    observation ObservationEvent (0..*) <"Captures a recorded market event, including date, time, price, rate type, and source, often used in derivatives pricing or index calculations.">
    reset ResetEvent (0..*) <"Defines the periodic adjustment of a trade\'s rate or value, specifying the reference trade, date, calculated reset value, and any relevant details affecting financial terms.">
    additionalEvent AdditionalEvent (0..1)
    optionExercise OptionExercise (0..1) <"A structure describing an option exercise event. The optionExercise event supports partial exercise (specify the number of options or amount to exercise), full exercise (use fullExercise flag), as well as the option to request options not to be exercised.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

    condition Choice:
        if trade exists
        then tradePackage is absent
                and amendment is absent
                and increase is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and termination is absent
                and novation is absent
                and withdrawal is absent
                and observation is absent
                and reset is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if amendment exists
        then increase is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and termination is absent
                and novation is absent
                and withdrawal is absent
                and observation is absent
                and reset is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if increase exists
        then terminatingEvent is absent
                and termination is absent
                and novation is absent
                and withdrawal is absent
                and observation is absent
                and reset is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if termination exists
        then novation is absent
                and withdrawal is absent
                and observation is absent
                and reset is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if novation exists
        then terminatingEvent is absent
                and withdrawal is absent
                and observation is absent
                and reset is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if withdrawal exists
        then terminatingEvent is absent
                and observation is absent
                and reset is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if observation exists
        then terminatingEvent is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if reset exists
        then terminatingEvent is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if additionalEvent exists
        then reset is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
                and optionExercise is absent
        else if optionExercise exists
        then reset is absent
                and additionalEvent is absent
                and tradePackage is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
                and terminatingEvent is absent
        else reset is absent
            and additionalEvent is absent
            and optionExercise is absent
            and originatingEvent is absent
            and terminatingEvent is absent

type EventRequestAcknowledgement extends ResponseMessage: <"Defines the structure for a message acknowledging an event request.">

    originalMessage UnprocessedElementWrapper (0..1) <"Contains the original event request message that was received and acknowledged. This ensures traceability by retaining the initial request, even if it has not yet been fully processed. Given its type UnprocessedElementWrapper, it serves as a container for the unprocessed or partially processed event request, which is typically used to encapsulate raw XML content or messages that require further validation or transformation before they can be fully interpreted.">
    tradeReferenceInformation TradeReferenceInformation (0..1) <"Information about a trade.">
    party Party (0..*) <"A legal entity or a subdivision of a legal entity. Parties can perform multiple roles in a trade lifecycle. For example, the principal parties obligated to make payments from time to time during the term of the trade, but may include other parties involved in, or incidental to, the trade, such as parties acting in the role of novation transferor/transferee, broker, calculation agent, etc. In FpML roles are defined in multiple places within a document.">
    account Account (0..*) <"Optional account information used to precisely define the origination and destination of financial instruments.">

type RequestedCollateralAllocationAction: <"A type that describes the type of collateral allocation action that is requested. The purpose is to allow FCMs to specify how the allocations are to be processed.">

    value Scheme (1..1)
    requestedCollateralAllocationActionScheme NonEmptyURI (0..1)

type TradeWrapper: <"A structure that contains a business event.">

    originatingEvent OriginatingEvent (0..1) <"This may be used to describe why a trade was created. This can be used to provide context for a newly created trade that is not part of a post-trade event. For example, it can report that the trade was created as a result of netting activity, or due to a transfer, an allocation process, etc. Omitting this implies that the trade record was created as a result of a negotiated new trade.">
    trade Trade (0..1) <"A financial transaction, including its contractual details, counterparties, risk parameters, and governing agreements. It serves as the primary record of an executed trade.">
    tradeReferenceInformation TradeReferenceInformation (0..1) <"Information about a trade.">
    tradePackage TradePackage (0..1) <"A collection of trades or trade-related references under a unified structure, facilitating bulk processing, aggregation, or operational handling of multiple transactions.">

    condition Choice:
        if trade exists
        then tradeReferenceInformation is absent and tradePackage is absent
        else if tradeReferenceInformation exists
        then trade is absent and originatingEvent is absent and tradePackage is absent
        else if tradePackage exists
        then trade is absent
                and tradeReferenceInformation is absent
                and originatingEvent is absent
        else False
